  "_meta": {
    "scenario": "delay-off-scaled-light",
    "notes": "The save has the delay feature switched off, so comms.delay reports a real APPLIED zero and there is no path total to apportion across the legs. The route is still worth annotating, and each leg's light-time comes from the save's own light speed, which this save has scaled to twice the real constant. Every leg therefore reads HALF the textbook light-time for its distance, which is the number the widget used to get wrong: it mirrored the speed of light as a client-side constant, and nothing on the wire could correct it. 1850km at 2c is 3.09ms; 640km at 2c is 1.07ms."
